    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe vim.pos / vim.range constructors and converters only say \"see |api-indexing|\", so from `K` you can't tell whether e.g. `vim.pos.cursor()` wants (1,0) or (0,0). `vim.range.to_mark()` also says it converts to an extmark range, but it returns a mark range.\n\n## Solution\n\nPut the indexing in each summary line, as suggested in the issue: (1,0) for cursor/mark, (0,0) for extmark, 0-based line plus encoding offset for lsp, 0-based byte offset for offset. Note that mark ranges are end-inclusive unless 'selection' is \"exclusive\", which is what `range.mark()` / `to_mark()` do. Fix the `to_mark()` wording.\n\nRef #39868. This doesn't touch the `see_lua` entries in eval.lua or any deprecations, those can be a follow-up.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-15T16:04:22Z",
